WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.012 line:82%
Chapter 4. Lessons. Your book is ready in the app.

00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:07.892 line:82%
Open "Lessons" in the menu.

00:00:08.353 --> 00:00:13.972 line:82%
The ready-made lessons of your book are here. You only see the books for the level of your class.

00:00:14.432 --> 00:00:22.011 line:82%
Press "Add". You get every grammar, vocabulary and function point of the book, each with a Test 1 and a Test 2.

00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:29.312 line:82%
The lessons are grouped by unit. The first card of each unit, with a coloured edge, is the unit test.

00:00:29.768 --> 00:00:33.211 line:82%
Type in the search box to find a lesson quickly.

00:00:33.664 --> 00:00:35.892 line:82%
Click a lesson to open it.

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:43.852 line:82%
Each lesson has four steps: Test 1 before you teach, then Teach, then Test 2 after you teach, and Compare.

00:00:44.309 --> 00:00:48.911 line:82%
These are the questions of Test 1. Click a question to open it.

00:00:49.364 --> 00:01:00.132 line:82%
Every question has 4 versions: the same skill, with a different sentence. Each class gets a different version, so students can't pass the answers to the next class.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:09.231 line:82%
Many questions have a photo. Students see it on the projector and on their phones. Press "Change photo" to choose another one.

00:01:09.684 --> 00:01:14.873 line:82%
Now let's make our own lesson. Go back to Lessons, and press "New lesson".

00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:17.731 line:82%
Write the title of the lesson.

00:01:18.584 --> 00:01:29.632 line:82%
Press "Add a question". There are about 20 types: multiple choice, true or false, gap fill, matching, find the mistake, sort into groups, listen and choose, and more.

00:01:30.091 --> 00:01:35.152 line:82%
Write the question and the options. Click the letter of the correct answer.

00:01:38.842 --> 00:01:46.492 line:82%
Add a skill tag, like "Present simple". The app uses it for the Skill map, and to compare Test 1 and Test 2.

00:01:46.956 --> 00:01:56.492 line:82%
Test settings are here: when students see the answer, the time for each question, mixed order, and surprises like double points and a lucky wheel.

00:01:56.943 --> 00:02:07.112 line:82%
Faster: import questions from Excel. With a Claude AI key, the app can also write questions for you. Everything is saved automatically.

00:02:07.576 --> 00:02:16.212 line:82%
Middle school? Each 1 AC, 2 AC and 3 AC class has its English Spotlight book. Here is a 1 AC class.

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:26.791 line:82%
Press "Add". One lesson for each lesson of the Student's Book, from the Welcome unit to Unit 6, with short sentences and many photos for beginners.

00:02:27.251 --> 00:02:35.831 line:82%
There are listening questions too. The laptop reads letters, numbers, times and dates aloud, and students choose what they hear.

00:02:36.298 --> 00:02:46.131 line:82%
Now the placement test. Back in Class A, the placement test is with the ready-made lessons. It has 40 questions, from easy to harder.

00:02:46.586 --> 00:02:53.292 line:82%
Use it at the start of the year, and again at the end. Press "Start a test", and choose "Start of year".

00:02:54.958 --> 00:03:04.770 line:82%
Students join as usual. Then press "Start the test". Each student answers at their own speed, with no timer, and never sees if they were right.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.731 line:82%
Your screen shows how far each student has got.

00:03:19.027 --> 00:03:29.432 line:82%
When everyone is done, press "Finish the test". Each student is put in a group: Strong, Average or Weak. Turn off the projector before you press "Show the groups"!

00:03:29.897 --> 00:03:38.411 line:82%
You see each student's score for grammar, vocabulary, functions and reading. The groups are also in Results, and in Excel.
